Asked: card two for b3-v1 — the one in and the one out, or no change — settling between Words of Wisdom for Stroke of Genius and Clever Concealment for Drift of Phantasms, with Alhammarret's Archive and Unwind/Rewind as alternates and every wheel off the list. The audit on the branch (Dawn's Truce already in) reads protection 4 against a 5-7 target and still under, card-advantage 15 against 10 and interaction 13 against 12-15 both at; the log's one recurring takeaway (001, 003) is Heliod removed before protection landed, and in 001 the counter that would have saved him was itself countered. So the draw-side candidates and the counterspells touch axes that are not binding, and the protection side is: Clever Concealment in, Drift of Phantasms out. Concealment phases out any number of your nonland permanents — Heliod, both Crawlers, Rhystic Study, Smothering Tithe, Teferi's Ageless Insight and the fort — against the shapes Dawn's Truce does not cover (exile-wipes, bounce, edicts, -X/-X, an uncounterable Supreme Verdict from across the table); Drift is the one tutor of the five whose fetch is an activated, sorcery-speed ability, so Heliod's discount and flash never touch it, and it is the slowest of nine Approach routes.

add_candidates: [{"card": "Clever Concealment", "closes": "protection", "source": "pool", "why": "{2}{W}{W} instant, convoke: any number of target nonland permanents you control phase out until your next turn. Protection reads 4 → 5, the low edge of target, and the fifth copy covers the shapes the first four do not: exile-wipes (Farewell, Sunfall, Merciless Eviction, an opponent's overloaded Winds of Abandon), bounce-wipes (Cyclonic Rift, Evacuation), edicts and -X/-X, and an uncounterable Supreme Verdict — for Heliod, Psychosis Crawler, Scrawling Crawler, Rhystic Study, Smothering Tithe, Teferi's Ageless Insight and the fort at once. Enumerated from card-search over WU non-Game-Changer instants not in the 99: thirteen phase-out instants, of which only Clever Concealment and Perch Protection phase out your permanents of every nonland type at once — Perch Protection at {4}{W}{W} with an extra turn gifted; Ripples of Potential needs counters on the permanents; Reality Ripple takes one artifact, creature or land and Vision Charm one artifact; Slip Out the Back, March of Swirling Mist, Galadriel's Dismissal and Change of Plans are creatures only; Sapphire Charm, Divine Smite and Teferi's Reproach act on an opponent's permanents; Time and Tide phases nothing of yours out; the hexproof-and-indestructible family (Flare of Fortitude, Restoration Magic's Curaga, Ultimate Magic: Holy, Surge of Salvation) duplicates Dawn's Truce and stops neither exile nor bounce nor an edict. Heliod discounts the {2};

cut_candidates: [{"card": "Drift of Phantasms", "why": "The one tutor of the five whose fetch is an activated ability ({1}{U}{U}, transmute only as a sorcery): Heliod's back face discounts spells and grants flash to spells, so the discount and the flash never reach it. Its transmute set in the branch is the fifteen other mana-value-3 nonland cards (Archmage's Charm, Blue Sun's Zenith, Dictate of Kruphix, Force of Negation, Ghostly Prison, Guardian of Faith, Long-Term Plans, Loran of the Third Path, Mirrormade, Propaganda, Rhystic Study, Scrawling Crawler, Solve the Equation, Stroke of Genius, Teferi, Time Raveler); Approach is two steps away through Solve the Equation or Long-Term Plans, the slowest of the nine routes. Propaganda, Ghostly Prison, Rhystic Study, Dictate, Mirrormade, Teferi and Scrawling Crawler are also reachable by Long-Term Plans (any card, third from top), so Drift is not the only tutor for a permanent — it is the only one that puts a permanent straight into hand.", "cost_of_cutting": "A 0/5 flying defender the fort can use as a blocker; the branch's only to-hand tutor for Rhystic Study, Propaganda, Ghostly Prison, Dictate of Kruphix, Mirrormade, Teferi, Time Raveler or Scrawling Crawler (Long-Term Plans reaches them third from top, Top and Scroll Rack accelerate that); one of two tutors for Scrawling Crawler, half of the audit's thinnest engine component (Psychosis Crawler or Scrawling Crawler drawn, size 2). Tutors read 4 instead of 5.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty"
